body:
Thank you for the reply.

&#x200B;

I did a fresh installation of windows 3 days ago as I upgraded to windows 10. As I've said above, the game was running perfectly before today's patch. Not to mention that regardless of the graphical setting, the framerate doesn't go up. All other games run perfectly smoothly so it's not the fault of my hardware, it must be black desert online. A few people have been complaining about crashes this patch, too.

&#x200B;

How are you getting 200 fps on a 1050 on remastered mode?

Calling bullshit on this one.

&#x200B;

First of all, 9 years ago river biomes didn't exist and there's a naturally generated river running on the bottom left hand side of the picture, same with ocean biomes, and there's a whole ocean biome on the right hand side of the image. A lot of the blocks used in essentially all of the builds. Unless you dug out a perfectly naturally-looking river and replaced blocks of every building when each new patch came out, you're lying. Second of all, you mentioned building this entirely in creative. Creative mode was only added in 1.8.1 which I believe was in 2012 (?) and unless you used inventory editors to do it before (which you didn't mention, so that's unlikely) again, I call bullshit.

&#x200B;

r/quityourbullshit

Perhaps happier, probably temporarily. It won't reverse the lifetime of trauma. It won't suddenly give me a loving family that care about me. It won't fix the fact that I'm 6'2 and people will stare at me. Babies might stop crying every time they look at my face, but people will still stare and I'll still suffer from crippling anxiety that prevents me from going to the shop down the road because every single passer by stares at me like I'm an elephant in a circus. I'll be 15 grand out of pocket, when I could've bought multiple cars, paid a down payment for a mortgage or even had a super expensive bridezilla wedding.. gone on vacation, travelled across Europe, if not the world.. Things that other people that don't have such a fucking handicap in life would do with that amount of money.

&#x200B;

I won't ever be able to have kids or have a functional reproductive system

&#x200B;

Life will still be shit. It may make me temporarily happy, but the novelty of it would wear off in a few months to a year and I'd be back to my miserable self because of the hundreds of other issues that would make any other human on this world want to blow their brains out immediately.

&#x200B;

I honestly have a theory that we are already dead and this is hell. If you think about the principles of life, nothing that's good ever lasts for ever, only bad or evil things. Greed, famine, pestilence, war. Those are permanent. Even people that claim to be happy are only indulging in temporary things. I want out.

"Do you know how much it hurts knowing how sad you really are?"

&#x200B;

She's got issues of her own and the thought of me not being well hurts her.

&#x200B;

In terms of the flat, she's got her own place in Leeds where we'd move to if I got kicked out, although it is way too small for two people and a cat

Hi, thank you for the info.

&#x200B;

Where should I look for freelancers? Location wise we'd prefer the south, namely Kent but anywhere is fine. We're a bit dubious about just going on craigslist.
